    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high-upside output today, anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (85.72), who remains our strongest play despite a 37% rain risk in his matchup against Ryan Feltner. The elite SP matchup against Feltner (5.05 xERA) significantly elevates the ceiling for **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** (75.64), both of whom benefit from favorable park factors and the pitcher\u2019s shaky expected performance. Similarly, **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.18) carries a strong projection thanks to a substantial SP skill edge against Robbie Ray, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Heliot Ramos** (70.19) are primary catalysts today; both players gain massive value from a +16% park boost, with **Heliot Ramos** further bolstered by a slow opposing delivery that keeps our stolen base aggressive mandate in play.\n\nWhile the core is set, the decision to bench **Miguel Vargas** (53.91) was the most difficult pivot. **Miguel Vargas** generated a respectable score thanks to favorable wind conditions and a strong xwOBA, but his matchup against Kevin Gausman\u2019s sub-4.00 xERA ultimately suppressed his efficiency compared to the high-volume hitters facing the softer rotations of Feltner and Baz. We are also monitoring **Jackson Merrill** (55.61) closely, as his negative platoon split against a lefty effectively forces him into the bottom tier of our starting nine. Owners should keep a close eye on the weather in the **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** game; should that 37% rain risk escalate into a delay or cancellation, our bench depth, specifically **Dominic Smith** or **Sam Antonacci**, will need to be ready to step in to preserve our daily roster efficiency.",
